00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:26,500
So in this lesson, I'm going to explain the importance of delta and volume.

21
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,100
First, we'll start with volume.

22
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:30,400
Why is volume more important than... price.

23
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:33,757
When institutional traders are moving size in the market, they

24
00:01:33,757 --> 00:01:36,899
try to hide their size, their volume, and not the price.

25
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,640
When you see price trade, you form an opinion of

26
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:43,300
the market, but when you see the volume, you see the facts of the market.

27
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:46,700
So let's think about that for a second.

28
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Why is volume more important than price?

29
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:53,000
Price is often viewed as an advertising mechanism.

30
00:01:53,400 --> 00:02:02,300
So, you know, imagine you're in the fruit market and you see apples on sale for,

31
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:05,504
you know, two for a

32
00:02:05,504 --> 00:02:06,908
dollar and you think, hey,

33
00:02:06,908 --> 00:02:09,998
that's a good price, you know, you want to buy it.

34
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:13,400
You're not... Concerned with what the volume is.

35
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:16,973
But if you know that there's going to be a

36
00:02:16,973 --> 00:02:20,146
big harvest and you like apples and you want to

37
00:02:20,146 --> 00:02:22,050
buy some extra to take home,

38
00:02:22,050 --> 00:02:28,397
you're going to think, well, I know that tomorrow there's going to be a lot of supply in the market.

39
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:31,400
Tomorrow the price might be $3 for a dollar.

40
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:38,200
So you might buy one pair today, but you can come back tomorrow and buy,

41
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,012
if you want to buy $5 worth,

42
00:02:41,012 --> 00:02:42,424
you could buy 10 today, but if

43
00:02:42,424 --> 00:02:45,956
you wait until tomorrow, you could buy 15 because it's going to be $3 for a dollar.

44
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:51,125
Trading in the markets is similar in that sense, where

45
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:53,545
say the S&Ps are offered at 1910 and

46
00:02:53,545 --> 00:02:59,596
you just see 50 on the offer, you kind of think the market's going to go higher and you're looking at

47
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,712
volume on the offer, you only

48
00:03:01,712 --> 00:03:03,593
see 50 lots, and you're thinking, well, if

49
00:03:03,593 --> 00:03:08,161
you get through that 50 lots, you know, the market can start to tick a little bit higher.

50
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:12,203
But if you know that the market is 1910 offered,

51
00:03:12,203 --> 00:03:14,616
but you see a size there of 1,000,

52
00:03:14,616 --> 00:03:18,409
are you going to have the same view of the market?

53
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:23,500
No, because you know there's a lot of supply there offered at 1910.

54
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,100
Let's take a look at a chart here real quick.

55
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:34,000
So this is an E-mini chart. And this is just measuring the volume.

56
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:42,700
You've seen the market trading between 1911 and 1913. And the volumes are going back and forth.

57
00:03:42,700 --> 00:03:45,500
It's this third line here, volume on the bottom.

58
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:56,900
You know, at this bar here at 1230, it's 4,500, 8,000 at 1236, 4,000 at 1237, 6,000 at 1240.

59
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:00,800
And then all of a sudden you see a big surge in the volume.

60
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:02,100
It almost doubles.

61
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:04,700
It goes to 13,000.

62
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:09,300
Back to 6,000, 8,000, jumps to 16,000 again, 7,000.

63
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:14,400
What you're seeing is a lot of supply coming into the market and the price selling off.

64
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,766
So obviously there's more inventory for sale

65
00:04:17,766 --> 00:04:20,532
and for people to move the inventory,

66
00:04:20,532 --> 00:04:23,298
they have to move the price down.

67
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:31,900
You know, volume has often been relegated to a secondary position by most traders. since they are focused on price.

68
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:36,600
Most indicators are designed around price.

69
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,700
They don't necessarily take into account volume.

70
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:43,700
Volume is useful for identifying turning points in the markets.

71
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:47,333
So in a downtrending market, sellers are

72
00:04:47,333 --> 00:04:51,399
usually in control, and for the market to turn, buyers need to take control.

73
00:04:51,900 --> 00:04:56,200
What that means is that buyers need to come in and overwhelm the sellers with demand.

74
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,400
There has to be more demand than supply.

75
00:04:59,900 --> 00:05:02,300
That's the basic rules of economics.

76
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,900
So here's an example in the crude oil.

77
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:09,200
The volume... Again, this is the third line here.

78
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:15,600
Starting at 952, you see volume of 400, 1400, 700, 800.

79
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:19,100
The market is just sort of trading sideways.

80
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:21,400
Then you're starting to see the volume really pick up again.

81
00:05:21,400 --> 00:05:25,400
1400, which is the highest for...

82
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:32,200
The most recent bars, 2,000, 1,200, as you see the market start to move away.

83
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,708
You're seeing additional buyers come in,

84
00:05:35,708 --> 00:05:38,916
and you're seeing buyers willing to

85
00:05:38,916 --> 00:05:44,798
buy the inventory that the sellers are offering to the market.

86
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:49,500
So in an uptrending market, buyers are usually in control.

87
00:05:49,600 --> 00:05:52,500
And for the market to turn, sellers need to take control.

88
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:56,000
What that means is that sellers need to come in and overwhelm the buyers with supply.

89
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:03,000
Which is, you know, the statement is the opposite of a downtrending market.

90
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,941
But in an uptrending market, you need to

91
00:06:06,941 --> 00:06:09,882
have either new supply come into the market

92
00:06:09,882 --> 00:06:16,499
or new sellers come into the market and offer inventory to the buyers that is going to overrun.

93
00:06:17,100 --> 00:06:18,954
The buying in the market for

94
00:06:18,954 --> 00:06:20,808
the market to start to sell

95
00:06:20,808 --> 00:06:22,662
off you're going to need more

96
00:06:22,662 --> 00:06:24,516
more sellers than buyers now that's

97
00:06:24,516 --> 00:06:30,697
in an uptrending market there's going to be times where there's just no more buyers but we're talking about how

98
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:34,700
you know how to read increasing and decreasing volume

99
00:06:38,184 --> 00:06:40,884
So, you know, let's get into Delta.

100
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:44,684
How can a trader measure volume in a way to trade in the short term?

101
00:06:45,184 --> 00:06:49,484
Well, there's this thing called delta that you're going to see on volume footprint charts.

102
00:06:50,084 --> 00:06:51,408
When prices start to move, the

103
00:06:51,408 --> 00:06:52,732
reason it moves is because of

104
00:06:52,732 --> 00:06:56,483
a series of aggressive buying or selling which will show up in the delta of a bar.

105
00:06:57,684 --> 00:07:00,784
Delta measures the strength of the market's auction process.

106
00:07:02,384 --> 00:07:04,584
The most important component of delta is volume.

107
00:07:05,384 --> 00:07:07,384
Volume must be understood in context of the market.

108
00:07:07,484 --> 00:07:09,529
When volume is expanding positively or

109
00:07:09,529 --> 00:07:11,574
negatively, a trader must watch its

110
00:07:11,574 --> 00:07:14,983
strength to fully comprehend the shift in supply and demand.

111
00:07:15,484 --> 00:07:18,884
It is important to note that delta does not take into account price.

112
00:07:26,244 --> 00:07:27,136
So delta,

113
00:07:27,136 --> 00:07:29,812
you know, I explained briefly in

114
00:07:29,812 --> 00:07:32,488
the terms section what delta is

115
00:07:32,488 --> 00:07:37,841
and what the ask delta is and what the bid delta is.

116
00:07:38,444 --> 00:07:39,844
So now let's look at it on a chart.

117
00:07:40,844 --> 00:07:45,344
So you have down here at the bottom, you have the ask, the bid, and the delta.

118
00:07:45,344 --> 00:07:50,444
This is actually the ask delta. The bid delta and the net delta for the bar.

119
00:07:50,844 --> 00:07:56,444
So when you have an ask delta, that's the volume that's traded on the offer.

120
00:07:56,744 --> 00:07:58,844
The bid delta is what's traded on the bid.

121
00:07:58,844 --> 00:08:02,144
So we'll take a look at this bar right here at 812.

122
00:08:03,044 --> 00:08:09,144
So you see 374. That's if you take all the volume traded on the offer, add it together, you get 374.

123
00:08:09,844 --> 00:08:15,944
On the bid side, you get 1432. If you take all the numbers traded on the bid side, you get 1432.

124
00:08:16,244 --> 00:08:23,444
When you subtract the 374 from 1432, you get negative 1058.

125
00:08:23,544 --> 00:08:25,344
So you have a negative delta in the bar.

126
00:08:26,744 --> 00:08:32,544
And what that's telling you is that there was more sold into the bid than bought on the offer.

127
00:08:39,776 --> 00:08:46,976
Now, with most footprint charts, you can choose to have the bid and the ask

128
00:08:47,976 --> 00:08:49,649
deltas in there, or you

129
00:08:49,649 --> 00:08:51,992
can just, like on this chart, not

130
00:08:51,992 --> 00:08:55,674
have it in there and just concentrate on the net deltas.

131
00:08:57,276 --> 00:09:00,176
It's personal preference whether you want to have it or not.

132
00:09:04,976 --> 00:09:07,651
Once you start looking at deltas fairly regularly,

133
00:09:07,651 --> 00:09:10,326
you're going to get used to understanding the

134
00:09:10,326 --> 00:09:15,676
numbers, and you might just want to go with where you just have the net delta.

135
00:09:18,176 --> 00:09:20,276
Delta is overlooked by most traders.

136
00:09:20,376 --> 00:09:23,376
The only traders who follow Delta are mainly order flow traders.

137
00:09:23,676 --> 00:09:25,476
Delta is not used by most

138
00:09:25,476 --> 00:09:27,276
traders because most people, they don't

139
00:09:27,276 --> 00:09:29,076
even know it exists, let alone

140
00:09:29,076 --> 00:09:32,376
how to read it and understand it and trade with it.

141
00:09:35,376 --> 00:09:37,344
Now, Delta can alert you to

142
00:09:37,344 --> 00:09:39,968
areas in the market when buyers are drying

143
00:09:39,968 --> 00:09:43,576
up in an up move and where sellers are getting stronger.

144
00:09:45,376 --> 00:09:49,676
Delta alerts you to areas where sellers are getting less in a down move and buyers are starting to dominate.

145
00:09:49,976 --> 00:09:52,376
This is what causes changes in trends.

146
00:09:54,848 --> 00:09:57,748
Okay, so I'll show you a nice example here.

147
00:09:58,348 --> 00:09:58,648
Um,

148
00:10:00,248 --> 00:10:09,548
If you're watching the delta, which is the top line here, you're seeing minus deltas here, minus 723, minus 912.

149
00:10:09,948 --> 00:10:17,948
Now you've got a positive delta of 758. Then a positive delta of 2,000, and then again a positive delta of 2,600.

150
00:10:18,448 --> 00:10:21,095
What you're seeing is this market is

151
00:10:21,095 --> 00:10:23,742
going sideways for the most part, but

152
00:10:23,742 --> 00:10:27,146
you're seeing the deltas really starting to turn positive.

153
00:10:27,448 --> 00:10:29,148
Buyers are starting to take control.

154
00:10:29,548 --> 00:10:33,948
You've got three bars here with positive delta, fairly strong positive deltas.

155
00:10:35,148 --> 00:10:37,948
What that's telling you, buying has come in.

156
00:10:37,948 --> 00:10:39,638
Buyers are starting to overwhelm

157
00:10:39,638 --> 00:10:45,047
the sellers. They're willing to pay the offer price to try and take the market higher.

158
00:10:45,448 --> 00:10:50,548
And you see, we're starting to string together more positive deltas as the markets are moving higher.

159
00:10:51,748 --> 00:11:00,648
If these deltas and these bars were just sort of average numbers, maybe 700, 900, the market may continue to go sideways.

160
00:11:00,648 --> 00:11:04,148
But what you're seeing here is very strong positive deltas.

161
00:11:04,248 --> 00:11:11,148
You're seeing 2,000, 2,600, when earlier you're just seeing deltas in the 700, 900 levels.

162
00:11:12,948 --> 00:11:15,648
Buyers are really starting to overwhelm the sellers here.

163
00:11:20,112 --> 00:11:22,012
Here's an example of a market that's selling off.

164
00:11:22,112 --> 00:11:26,512
We've got some positive deltas here, you know, 2,000, 1,800.

165
00:11:27,312 --> 00:11:32,112
Here you have 1,900 in this third bar, then 2,000 again.

166
00:11:32,712 --> 00:11:33,800
You know, so

167
00:11:33,800 --> 00:11:35,614
it's these deltas, you know,

168
00:11:35,614 --> 00:11:37,428
they sort of mirror the

169
00:11:37,428 --> 00:11:39,242
other, you know, previous deltas,

170
00:11:39,242 --> 00:11:42,508
you know, more or less as you're going sideways.

171
00:11:42,912 --> 00:11:44,312
But as you start to break out,

172
00:11:45,112 --> 00:11:46,062
you know, of

173
00:11:46,062 --> 00:11:48,278
this lower area of this green bar

174
00:11:48,278 --> 00:11:50,178
at 1907, and you hit it in

175
00:11:50,178 --> 00:11:53,661
this red bar at 1048 where you got 2,000, you're seeing the deltas

176
00:11:55,112 --> 00:12:02,612
still remaining very strong, you know, 3,000, 2,000, 3,000, as the market sells off.

177
00:12:03,712 --> 00:12:08,112
You're seeing in this case, this is where the sellers are taking control of the market.

178
00:12:08,312 --> 00:12:09,236
You know, the

179
00:12:09,236 --> 00:12:10,776
deltas oftentimes, you know, they'll

180
00:12:10,776 --> 00:12:12,932
go positive. You know, you'll get one

181
00:12:12,932 --> 00:12:16,012
or two positive, one or two negative, back and forth.

182
00:12:16,012 --> 00:12:19,242
But when you're starting to string together a series of

183
00:12:19,242 --> 00:12:21,503
negative deltas, look for the market to

184
00:12:21,503 --> 00:12:24,410
start to sell off if you string it together.

185
00:12:25,212 --> 00:12:33,012
Series of positive deltas, you know, look for the market to start to, you know, start to rally.

186
00:12:35,424 --> 00:12:38,124
So what drives price movements in the market?

187
00:12:38,224 --> 00:12:40,124
Well, it's the differences of opinion.

188
00:12:40,224 --> 00:12:42,171
When a market is trading as per

189
00:12:42,171 --> 00:12:43,562
normal, at equilibrium, so to

190
00:12:43,562 --> 00:12:46,622
speak, the delta should be relatively low or not changing much.

191
00:12:46,624 --> 00:12:49,924
Supply and demand at that point is about equal.

192
00:12:51,024 --> 00:12:56,524
The problem is no one knows where this level of equilibrium is. It constantly changes.

193
00:12:57,224 --> 00:13:00,524
Delta tracks a difference of opinion and more importantly how it's changing.

194
00:13:00,624 --> 00:13:03,424
Delta shows you exactly how strong buyers or sellers are.

195
00:13:03,824 --> 00:13:10,524
Delta shows you when the market is calm and the market is facilitating trade, which is its main purpose.

196
00:13:12,424 --> 00:13:15,624
So for example, this is

197
00:13:17,824 --> 00:13:21,024
a chart of the E-minis.

198
00:13:26,524 --> 00:13:32,524
So in this chart of the ES, you'll see the market has been rallying, going up, up, up.

199
00:13:32,924 --> 00:13:35,724
We hit a high up here in this bar at

200
00:13:35,724 --> 00:13:39,644
1043. It's got a small negative delta following a bar with a big positive delta.

201
00:13:40,524 --> 00:13:45,624
Then it sort of goes sideways. The market goes sideways over the next few bars.

202
00:13:45,924 --> 00:13:50,824
We have this bar at the high with a delta of minus 92.

203
00:13:51,224 --> 00:13:53,824
The bar follows it with a delta of minus 49.

204
00:13:54,324 --> 00:13:56,724
Then the next bar is minus 275.

205
00:13:56,824 --> 00:14:00,424
The next bar is positive 174 and a positive 187.

206
00:14:01,524 --> 00:14:06,424
And over here at 1051, you got a delta of minus 612.

207
00:14:07,824 --> 00:14:09,724
So you got to take into account what's happening.

208
00:14:09,824 --> 00:14:11,024
Think about what just happened.

209
00:14:11,024 --> 00:14:15,024
The market is going up, and then it goes sideways.

210
00:14:15,024 --> 00:14:18,024
And as it's going sideways, the deltas are...

211
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:25,224
Fairly small, you know, minus 90, minus 50, minus 200, plus 170, plus 187.

212
00:14:26,224 --> 00:14:28,724
And why isn't the market not going anywhere?

213
00:14:28,724 --> 00:14:29,624
It's going sideways.

214
00:14:29,624 --> 00:14:34,924
What this is telling you, these small deltas, is that the buying and selling is evenly distributed.

215
00:14:35,024 --> 00:14:35,924
And why is that important?

216
00:14:36,024 --> 00:14:36,324
Well,

217
00:14:37,124 --> 00:14:37,924
We're at a high.

218
00:14:38,224 --> 00:14:42,288
If the market is going to continue going high, you want to

219
00:14:42,288 --> 00:14:44,997
see strong positive deltas, not evenly distributed deltas

220
00:14:44,997 --> 00:14:48,722
where the buying and selling is matched for the most part.

221
00:14:49,224 --> 00:14:56,524
When you start moving out of this range, this area, you see the delta start getting bigger, minus 600.

222
00:14:57,024 --> 00:15:00,624
Then at 1052, it's minus 2336.

223
00:15:00,624 --> 00:15:01,824
You got a selling imbalance.

224
00:15:02,324 --> 00:15:04,524
You could see now that the sellers have taken over.

225
00:15:04,624 --> 00:15:06,924
They've overrun the buyers.

226
00:15:10,024 --> 00:15:11,624
And the market just sold right off.

227
00:15:12,124 --> 00:15:15,957
This area up here where it's just going sideways, some

228
00:15:15,957 --> 00:15:19,023
people like to call that absorption, where buying

229
00:15:19,023 --> 00:15:23,623
and selling is evenly matched, and the market is basically going sideways.

230
00:15:28,316 --> 00:15:31,239
So one of the main reasons so many traders lose money or fail at

231
00:15:31,239 --> 00:15:32,491
trading is because they come into

232
00:15:32,491 --> 00:15:35,414
the market thinking all they have to do is buy low and sell high.

233
00:15:35,916 --> 00:15:40,254
Oftentimes they are buying only to have the market keep dropping after

234
00:15:40,254 --> 00:15:45,315
they have bought or sold and the market keeps on going higher against them.

235
00:15:47,316 --> 00:15:48,316
In theory, it's simple.

236
00:15:48,416 --> 00:15:50,116
I'll just buy low and sell high.

237
00:15:50,116 --> 00:15:54,116
But how often have you bought and then the market just keeps dropping?

238
00:15:54,216 --> 00:15:55,924
Or how often have you sold thinking

239
00:15:55,924 --> 00:15:57,632
this is the high or the end

240
00:15:57,632 --> 00:16:00,316
of a move and the market just keeps going against you?

241
00:16:01,416 --> 00:16:05,916
What successful traders do is buy when the market is showing strength and sell when the market is weak.

242
00:16:06,416 --> 00:16:10,516
The successful traders buy high and sell higher, or they sell low and buy lower.

243
00:16:11,116 --> 00:16:12,516
You have to think like a mercenary.

244
00:16:12,716 --> 00:16:16,616
Yeah, I know that sounds cliche, but you want to fight on the side that is winning.

245
00:16:17,016 --> 00:16:18,561
You don't want to waste your time

246
00:16:18,561 --> 00:16:19,665
trying to fight a losing

247
00:16:19,665 --> 00:16:22,315
battle, trying to pick highs and lows, trying to gain some glory.

248
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:27,588
If you can see by the order flow that the market is

249
00:16:27,588 --> 00:16:32,216
starting to show some strength in the form of buying or show weakness,

250
00:16:34,116 --> 00:16:39,716
in the fact that vine has dried up, that's the way you want to go.

251
00:16:40,516 --> 00:16:42,092
You don't want to sell it just because

252
00:16:42,092 --> 00:16:43,471
we made a new high or you

253
00:16:43,471 --> 00:16:47,215
don't want to buy just because you made a new low, thinking this is going to be the bottom.

254
00:16:47,616 --> 00:16:52,316
You just wait. Wait for the opportunity. Wait for the market to tell you what it's going to do.

255
00:16:53,016 --> 00:16:56,516
Most of the time, The market isn't going to be telling you anything.

256
00:16:56,616 --> 00:16:59,222
It's just going to be doing what

257
00:16:59,222 --> 00:17:01,828
it does in trading, facilitating the buying

258
00:17:01,828 --> 00:17:07,414
and selling of market and the transfer of goods from one hand to the other.

259
00:17:07,416 --> 00:17:09,460
But there's going to be times when

260
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,504
it's very, very obvious, and you can

261
00:17:11,504 --> 00:17:14,716
see that in the order flow and especially in the delta.

262
00:17:17,416 --> 00:17:20,016
So here's a chart of crude oil, right?

263
00:17:20,116 --> 00:17:28,416
And as you're going down, you're seeing the deltas strongly negative, you know, minus 190, minus 299, minus 495.

264
00:17:28,616 --> 00:17:32,716
That's what you want to see when the market is showing strength on a move to the downside.

265
00:17:33,016 --> 00:17:34,316
The market sort of goes sideways.

266
00:17:34,316 --> 00:17:40,216
You can see the deltas, you know, minus 100, plus 40, minus 49, minus 53 as the market goes sideways.

267
00:17:42,816 --> 00:17:43,716
Think about what just happened.

268
00:17:43,716 --> 00:17:45,441
We sold off, so there could

269
00:17:45,441 --> 00:17:47,166
be some profit taking coming in

270
00:17:47,166 --> 00:17:50,616
there to sort of meet with the selling, people covering their shorts.

271
00:17:51,216 --> 00:17:55,016
Then once those buyers are done, the market continues down.

272
00:17:55,016 --> 00:18:02,616
You can see again the delta is picking up strength, minus 226, minus 303, minus 287 as the market moves down.

273
00:18:06,488 --> 00:18:10,788
Okay, this is an E-mini chart. And for the most part, the market's going sideways.

274
00:18:10,788 --> 00:18:17,388
And what do you have? You've got relatively small deltas, 168, 200, 60, 95.

275
00:18:17,788 --> 00:18:25,188
I mean, you're going to get a few in here with some, you know, Decent numbers, 411, 693, 400.

276
00:18:25,688 --> 00:18:27,388
The market is just going sideways.

277
00:18:27,788 --> 00:18:32,588
You know, just when it goes sideways, it's not always just going to be, you know, small numbers.

278
00:18:33,488 --> 00:18:37,288
You know, you're not going to get somewhere where people try to push it down or push it up.

279
00:18:37,688 --> 00:18:40,688
But there's no follow-through in the next bar.

280
00:18:41,188 --> 00:18:44,488
It's, you know, the market is telling you that it's going sideways.

281
00:18:44,488 --> 00:18:47,270
It's when you start breaking out and start

282
00:18:47,270 --> 00:18:49,704
stringing together strong deltas in one direction,

283
00:18:49,704 --> 00:18:51,790
like here you've got minus 400, minus 500.

284
00:18:53,488 --> 00:18:54,902
Minus 1400 and right as the

285
00:18:54,902 --> 00:18:57,165
market starts to sell off that's you know

286
00:18:57,165 --> 00:18:59,428
this is the sign in the market that

287
00:18:59,428 --> 00:19:04,803
you're looking to to see on a regular basis and it does appear every day in almost every market

288
00:19:06,288 --> 00:19:07,472
you know here you

289
00:19:07,472 --> 00:19:08,952
know earlier you got minus 411

290
00:19:08,952 --> 00:19:10,728
delta but then immediately the next

291
00:19:10,728 --> 00:19:13,096
bar you got a positive delta oh you

292
00:19:13,096 --> 00:19:14,872
know if the selling is going

293
00:19:14,872 --> 00:19:20,496
to continue you're going to be looking for you know a strong negative delta then again you know minus 600

294
00:19:21,888 --> 00:19:23,001
93 you're thinking hey this

295
00:19:23,001 --> 00:19:24,948
could be the start of it but

296
00:19:24,948 --> 00:19:28,008
what happens the next bar you get a small positive delta

297
00:19:29,288 --> 00:19:31,288
Then it starts to reappear shortly thereafter.

298
00:19:31,288 --> 00:19:33,088
But, you know, at this time, you know, I had to get it.

299
00:19:33,188 --> 00:19:33,755
short, you

300
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:34,890
know, depending on how

301
00:19:34,890 --> 00:19:36,025
tight your stop is,

302
00:19:36,025 --> 00:19:37,160
maybe you get stopped

303
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,295
out or, you know,

304
00:19:38,295 --> 00:19:43,686
take a small, you know, a small loss or, you know, scratch it and think you got to reassess.

305
00:19:44,088 --> 00:19:45,221
But then, you know,

306
00:19:45,221 --> 00:19:46,921
the next couple bars, it's really

307
00:19:46,921 --> 00:19:48,337
clear to you that, hey,

308
00:19:48,337 --> 00:19:50,887
the sell-off, you want to get in on it.

309
00:19:55,388 --> 00:19:57,788
Okay, and again, this is the bond chart.

310
00:19:58,488 --> 00:19:59,388
What do you have here?

311
00:20:00,088 --> 00:20:08,088
You've got a market going sideways. It's not showing the deltas here, but you've got minus 200, minus 400, minus 500.

312
00:20:08,388 --> 00:20:09,688
The market's not going down.

313
00:20:10,188 --> 00:20:17,588
You've got three fairly strong negative deltas. They're increasing in size, but why isn't the market going down?

314
00:20:18,488 --> 00:20:22,488
In this bar at 824, you got a positive delta of 85.

315
00:20:22,488 --> 00:20:29,388
Okay, it's not the biggest positive delta, thinking that the supply and demand has shifted.

316
00:20:30,188 --> 00:20:35,388
But it's a sign. It's telling you. hey, there's buying in here.

317
00:20:35,688 --> 00:20:40,488
It's kind of disguised with the small delta, but you can see it in there.

318
00:20:41,388 --> 00:20:45,088
The sellers were met with good buyers.

319
00:20:45,388 --> 00:20:47,688
Then the next bar, again, it's a positive delta.

320
00:20:47,688 --> 00:20:51,788
It's starting to build on this positive delta from the bar earlier.

321
00:20:52,688 --> 00:21:00,588
Again, you have these three bars here with negative delta that's growing, but why isn't the market going down?

322
00:21:00,588 --> 00:21:06,488
This is what you have to be asking yourself. and noticing it when the market is trading.

323
00:21:07,188 --> 00:21:12,588
You can see here, this is really the shift, the change in demand.

324
00:21:12,988 --> 00:21:15,688
Before, there's a lot of supply. It's being sold in there.

325
00:21:16,988 --> 00:21:18,188
It's met with buyers.

326
00:21:18,888 --> 00:21:22,188
And here, now you're starting to see the buyers take over from the sellers.

327
00:21:22,888 --> 00:21:29,988
And you see 85, 149, 426, 1900 as the market is pulling away from this area.

328
00:21:30,488 --> 00:21:31,488
That's what you're looking for.

329
00:21:31,488 --> 00:21:37,388
You're looking for signs that the buyers have taken over from the sellers.

330
00:21:38,488 --> 00:21:40,188
Here it was dominated by sellers.

331
00:21:40,288 --> 00:21:42,088
The market necessarily wasn't moving anywhere.

332
00:21:42,188 --> 00:21:44,188
It wasn't going down when you're seeing these deltas.

333
00:21:45,188 --> 00:21:45,988
It's just hanging around.

334
00:21:45,988 --> 00:21:49,988
You've got a small delta. You know, a delta of 85 is fairly small.

335
00:21:50,088 --> 00:21:52,188
You know, it could be a difference of one trade, actually.

336
00:21:53,688 --> 00:21:58,588
You know, for me, I tend to find it kind of neutral when I see a smaller delta number.

337
00:21:58,788 --> 00:22:00,321
It could easily have gone the other

338
00:22:00,321 --> 00:22:01,854
way had there been a little bit

339
00:22:01,854 --> 00:22:03,387
more volume in that bar to trade.

340
00:22:03,888 --> 00:22:09,588
But nevertheless, you know, it's positive, and it's starting to build on it in the next couple of bars.

341
00:22:09,788 --> 00:22:11,428
And, you know, you see

342
00:22:11,428 --> 00:22:13,724
the big positive delta come in here

343
00:22:13,724 --> 00:22:17,660
at 841, you know, as the market is really moving in that direction.

344
00:22:21,848 --> 00:22:25,648
So when looking at delta, there are basically five scenarios when it comes to delta in a bar.

345
00:22:25,748 --> 00:22:29,748
It could be an extremely positive number, indicates aggressive buyers have dominated the bar.

346
00:22:30,548 --> 00:22:34,748
Buyers are buying all the available supply offered by sellers and moving the market higher.

347
00:22:34,848 --> 00:22:41,648
What I mean by extremely positive delta, usually it's something, you know, over 1,000 or more.

348
00:22:43,248 --> 00:22:48,548
Average positive delta number would indicate aggressive buyers outnumber sellers, but not overwhelmingly.

349
00:22:48,948 --> 00:22:54,448
This can be a sign of accumulation when a series of average positive delta bars are being put together.

350
00:22:55,948 --> 00:23:03,948
For example, you should know what sort of deltas you'll see in your normal market, depending on what you trade.

351
00:23:05,248 --> 00:23:06,448
For the E-minis,

352
00:23:08,348 --> 00:23:16,648
Usually when you see deltas over 5,000 or 6,000, that's an extremely positive delta number.

353
00:23:17,048 --> 00:23:26,348
When you see deltas around 1,000, 900, 1,000, anywhere between 500 and 1,500, it's kind of an average positive delta number.

354
00:23:27,148 --> 00:23:30,548
It's just telling you there was slightly more buying than selling in the bar.

355
00:23:31,748 --> 00:23:37,748
A small or negative delta number that's close to zero indicates aggressive buyers and sellers are pretty much evenly matched.

356
00:23:37,748 --> 00:23:41,648
Prices at equilibrium, both buyers and sellers are happy to trade at.

357
00:23:42,448 --> 00:23:48,048
What I consider that is a number less than 100, either positive or negative.

358
00:23:48,448 --> 00:23:51,648
because, you know, I said it's rare.

359
00:23:51,748 --> 00:23:54,719
You do get zero deltas in a bar

360
00:23:54,719 --> 00:23:57,690
where it's perfectly matched, but, you know, sometimes

361
00:23:57,690 --> 00:24:01,032
you're going to get a delta of 6 or 30 or 87,

362
00:24:03,148 --> 00:24:04,568
you know, especially when the

363
00:24:04,568 --> 00:24:06,556
bar has, you know, a total volume

364
00:24:06,556 --> 00:24:07,976
of, say, 8,000 lots that traded

365
00:24:07,976 --> 00:24:09,680
and the delta is, you know, 70.

366
00:24:10,848 --> 00:24:12,048
You know, it's telling you...

367
00:24:12,448 --> 00:24:15,848
That the buying and selling is evenly matched.

368
00:24:17,048 --> 00:24:19,178
I tend to take it, whether it's

369
00:24:19,178 --> 00:24:21,308
positive or negative, in the same light.

370
00:24:21,308 --> 00:24:24,047
I sort of treat it as a neutral delta.

371
00:24:25,548 --> 00:24:32,548
So an average negative delta number indicates aggressive sellers outnumber the aggressive buyers, not overwhelmingly.

372
00:24:32,848 --> 00:24:36,348
It can be a sign of steady reduction of position or shorts building up.

373
00:24:36,648 --> 00:24:38,441
An average negative delta number

374
00:24:38,441 --> 00:24:40,234
would be something, you know,

375
00:24:40,234 --> 00:24:42,027
minus 500 to, you know, minus 1500,

376
00:24:42,027 --> 00:24:45,613
just as an average positive delta would be around 500 to 1500.

377
00:24:47,848 --> 00:24:52,148
An extremely negative delta number indicates aggressive sellers have dominated the bar.

378
00:24:52,248 --> 00:24:57,948
Sellers are basically hitting every bid as they dump their excess supply in expectation of lower prices.

379
00:24:58,448 --> 00:25:05,648
An extremely negative delta to me would be something along the lines of minus 4,000, minus 5,000 and above.

380
00:25:06,748 --> 00:25:08,448
That's fairly obvious.

381
00:25:08,648 --> 00:25:14,548
Everyone's rushing in to sell as much as they can in expectation that the market is going lower.

382
00:25:16,048 --> 00:25:18,748
Just a quick couple points. points.

383
00:25:18,848 --> 00:25:20,948
Actually, delta does not take into account price.

384
00:25:20,948 --> 00:25:22,224
It doesn't, you know,

385
00:25:22,224 --> 00:25:24,139
you don't even, when you're looking

386
00:25:24,139 --> 00:25:26,054
at delta, you're not really concerned

387
00:25:26,054 --> 00:25:29,246
about the price of the market where it's trading at.

388
00:25:30,148 --> 00:25:33,848
Really, all you're concerned about is the net difference between the buyers and the sellers.

389
00:25:34,748 --> 00:25:38,148
When the delta is negative and price is going up, be careful.

390
00:25:38,948 --> 00:25:43,348
Why is price going up while the delta is negative?

391
00:25:43,648 --> 00:25:49,420
Well, it could be a couple of things. The main one is it could be support

392
00:25:49,420 --> 00:25:51,992
in the market and people are trying to

393
00:25:51,992 --> 00:25:53,921
push the market down and they're

394
00:25:53,921 --> 00:25:55,850
basically hitting the bids, but there

395
00:25:55,850 --> 00:25:58,744
could be somebody in there with a lot of...

396
00:25:59,048 --> 00:26:00,448
You know, a lot

397
00:26:00,448 --> 00:26:03,248
of demand, a big passive buyer that, you

398
00:26:03,248 --> 00:26:08,148
know, they're basically willing to buy as much as people are willing to sell.

399
00:26:08,448 --> 00:26:10,203
And then when those sellers are

400
00:26:10,203 --> 00:26:12,543
done, you know, they've got no more bullets

401
00:26:12,543 --> 00:26:16,346
left, so to speak, you know, the market will pop up a bit.

402
00:26:17,348 --> 00:26:23,248
And, you know, the opposite is true. When delta is positive, and price is going down, again, be careful.

403
00:26:23,648 --> 00:26:25,319
You know, when delta is positive,

404
00:26:25,319 --> 00:26:26,990
you have more buying than selling.

405
00:26:26,990 --> 00:26:31,447
So if price is going down, you know, it shouldn't be. It should be going up.

406
00:26:32,948 --> 00:26:37,248
You know, and just to, you know, further example.

407
00:26:38,348 --> 00:26:43,748
Now this is the chart we had earlier it looks like and actually no, this is a slightly different one.

408
00:26:43,748 --> 00:26:46,648
This is crude oil and what's happening?

409
00:26:46,748 --> 00:26:50,248
We're going up, up, up and you got negative deltas all on the way up.

410
00:26:51,848 --> 00:26:55,348
Well, why? You know, if you're going up, you should have positive deltas.

411
00:26:55,948 --> 00:26:57,773
One, it's usually a function that,

412
00:26:57,773 --> 00:27:00,206
you know, there's offers on the way up

413
00:27:00,206 --> 00:27:03,247
that people are buying in expectation of the move higher.

414
00:27:03,748 --> 00:27:04,048
Well,

415
00:27:06,848 --> 00:27:09,248
What they're doing, basically, they're buying the available supply.

416
00:27:09,548 --> 00:27:15,648
At some point when those buyers have bought all that they need, what's going to happen?

417
00:27:16,848 --> 00:27:19,348
It's not like the market is just going to keep going up and up and up.

418
00:27:20,248 --> 00:27:23,067
If the sellers are going to come in

419
00:27:23,067 --> 00:27:27,647
and start hitting the bids on the way up, as people are bidding,

420
00:27:28,548 --> 00:27:31,148
Here you have 392, 323.

421
00:27:31,448 --> 00:27:36,848
You're seeing on the bid side, big strong bids, 369, 420.

422
00:27:36,848 --> 00:27:38,048
Someone is supporting the market.

423
00:27:38,348 --> 00:27:40,929
People are trying to sell it to move

424
00:27:40,929 --> 00:27:42,865
it lower, but whoever is bidding

425
00:27:42,865 --> 00:27:45,446
just keeps moving, going slightly higher, higher, higher.

426
00:27:46,748 --> 00:27:48,293
And, you know, eventually,

427
00:27:48,293 --> 00:27:50,611
you know, these buyers, once they

428
00:27:50,611 --> 00:27:52,929
buy their, you know, buy what

429
00:27:52,929 --> 00:27:55,247
they need to buy, what happens?

430
00:27:56,248 --> 00:27:58,148
You know, they're no longer there to support the market.

431
00:27:58,148 --> 00:28:02,248
And then the sellers are going to come in and really start to move the market lower.

432
00:28:04,772 --> 00:28:12,672
You see here on the way up, you've got bid sides of 286, 390, 320, 369, 420.

433
00:28:12,972 --> 00:28:17,372
On the way down, where are these buyers that were here earlier?

434
00:28:18,272 --> 00:28:20,155
There's nothing more than, here's 277,

435
00:28:20,155 --> 00:28:22,038
229, but as it moves down,

436
00:28:22,038 --> 00:28:28,818
it moves down on much lesser volume than what you were seeing bidding it on the way up.

437
00:28:30,472 --> 00:28:34,372
You can see the deltas are, I said, you're going higher and you're getting negative deltas.

438
00:28:34,672 --> 00:28:38,872
So obviously there's people that are selling it and people that are buying it.

439
00:28:39,472 --> 00:28:41,572
They're working the bids and people are selling into the bids.

440
00:28:41,572 --> 00:28:44,072
But what's going to happen as you're up near the high?

441
00:28:44,072 --> 00:28:50,572
Eventually, these people that are buying it, that are supporting the market that people are selling into,

442
00:28:51,572 --> 00:28:52,372
You've got to watch.

443
00:28:55,072 --> 00:28:56,172
They're building their position.

444
00:28:56,272 --> 00:28:59,005
Once their position is built and they've

445
00:28:59,005 --> 00:29:04,471
got enough for their portfolio, they're not necessarily going to be buying it anymore.

446
00:29:04,472 --> 00:29:06,192
And then the market, you'll

447
00:29:06,192 --> 00:29:08,600
see a shift where as you start

448
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:13,072
to move lower, people are selling into the bid, sellers are taking over.

449
00:29:14,372 --> 00:29:16,006
But there's not much left in the bid

450
00:29:16,006 --> 00:29:19,071
side to really support the market as you were getting it on the way up.

451
00:29:24,340 --> 00:29:30,240
So understanding delta in relationship to where the market is trading can clue you into the possible reversals.

452
00:29:30,740 --> 00:29:35,140
When a market is hanging around the high, delta should be mostly positive.

453
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:38,740
When a market is hanging around a low, delta should be mostly negative.

454
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:42,540
When a market starts to move away from a higher low, delta can tip you off.

455
00:29:44,440 --> 00:29:49,140
Okay, for example, this is a Eurostock chart. You know, we're coming down into a low.

456
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:51,367
Here you have a divergence as

457
00:29:51,367 --> 00:29:52,385
this little arrow is.

458
00:29:52,385 --> 00:29:55,439
But, you know, on the way down, you got the negative deltas.

459
00:29:55,940 --> 00:29:57,625
And you hit the low, and

460
00:29:57,625 --> 00:29:58,748
what happens? You see

461
00:29:58,748 --> 00:30:01,838
a positive delta. That's what's telling you you've got a divergence.

462
00:30:01,840 --> 00:30:03,940
He's a new low and a positive delta.

463
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:06,740
At a low, you should have a negative delta.

464
00:30:06,840 --> 00:30:08,747
But then you start building up some more

465
00:30:08,747 --> 00:30:13,038
positive deltas over the next two or three bars, and the market starts moving away from the low.

466
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:16,440
This is what you're looking for as far as a reversal.

467
00:30:16,640 --> 00:30:23,440
You're looking for the low to be set, and you're looking for it to move away with positive deltas.

468
00:30:23,440 --> 00:30:27,840
You don't want to see more negative deltas coming in, more selling coming into the market.

469
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:36,240
And the reverse is true if you're going on your way up. You've got positive deltas on the way up.

470
00:30:36,540 --> 00:30:39,240
You hit the high, you got a divergence, you got a negative delta.

471
00:30:40,840 --> 00:30:43,640
And you've got the next bar after the high is negative delta.

472
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:46,040
The next bar after that is also negative delta.

473
00:30:46,140 --> 00:30:47,540
And you're moving away from the high.

474
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:53,140
When you come up to a high and you start putting in negative deltas, expect the market to sell off.

475
00:30:53,140 --> 00:30:58,640
People are taking this as the high, and they're reacting, and they're starting to sell at this level.

476
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:02,140
They feel this high is a good level to sell.

477
00:31:04,676 --> 00:31:12,376
Now, another way to interpret deltas is when you have massive delta numbers, they're either positive or negative.

478
00:31:12,376 --> 00:31:14,490
They're just so big, you find

479
00:31:14,490 --> 00:31:16,604
yourself saying, wow, they could tip

480
00:31:16,604 --> 00:31:19,775
you off to a short-term trend in that direction.

481
00:31:21,076 --> 00:31:28,976
For example, in a market that's trading relatively small, deltas, you know, a couple hundred aside.

482
00:31:29,376 --> 00:31:30,976
Like this is a crude oil chart, right?

483
00:31:31,176 --> 00:31:38,576
Most of the deltas, you see, you know, 200, 100, 189, 297, 267, you know, 500, 400 is pushing it.

484
00:31:38,876 --> 00:31:41,076
Here you got a big negative delta, minus 1,000.

485
00:31:41,676 --> 00:31:44,076
You've got, you know, selling imbalance right at that level.

486
00:31:45,376 --> 00:31:46,076
In that bar.

487
00:31:47,076 --> 00:31:47,826
You know, a

488
00:31:47,826 --> 00:31:49,576
thousand is considered, you know, like a

489
00:31:49,576 --> 00:31:51,326
wow level in the sense that, hey,

490
00:31:51,326 --> 00:31:53,076
wow, that's a lot, you know, don't

491
00:31:53,076 --> 00:31:54,576
miss this trade, you know, there's

492
00:31:54,576 --> 00:31:56,076
people looking to get short, especially,

493
00:31:56,076 --> 00:31:57,576
you know, after the high has

494
00:31:57,576 --> 00:32:00,076
been made, and all of a sudden you got big,

495
00:32:01,576 --> 00:32:02,896
you know, a big

496
00:32:02,896 --> 00:32:04,216
negative delta, a lot

497
00:32:04,216 --> 00:32:05,536
of selling came in,

498
00:32:05,536 --> 00:32:06,856
you know, you see,

499
00:32:06,856 --> 00:32:10,486
you know, 454, 538, you know, here, even in the imbalance, you got 165,

500
00:32:11,976 --> 00:32:17,376
243, there's obviously a lot of selling coming in, reacting to this high, you know, and the market sold off.

501
00:32:18,876 --> 00:32:19,854
You know, this

502
00:32:19,854 --> 00:32:21,158
is an E-mini chart,

503
00:32:21,158 --> 00:32:22,788
you know, we're trading around,

504
00:32:22,788 --> 00:32:24,745
you know, this level, going a

505
00:32:24,745 --> 00:32:26,702
little bit sideways here, then all

506
00:32:26,702 --> 00:32:31,921
of a sudden, you know, seeing what I consider average delta numbers, minus 1300, minus 854, then wham!

507
00:32:33,276 --> 00:32:37,176
you get hit with minus 5,000 delta.

508
00:32:38,076 --> 00:32:40,776
Even to the next bar, it came in as minus 3,800.

509
00:32:40,776 --> 00:32:43,504
But when you see a bar with very

510
00:32:43,504 --> 00:32:46,232
strong negative delta, it's markets tipping you off

511
00:32:46,232 --> 00:32:47,937
that, hey, there's a lot

512
00:32:47,937 --> 00:32:50,324
of sellers that overwhelm these buyers that

513
00:32:50,324 --> 00:32:54,075
were sitting down here on the bid side in the bar.

514
00:32:55,376 --> 00:33:02,576
And the market had a little change. In this case, it was a continuation of the trend.

515
00:33:02,576 --> 00:33:04,059
Oftentimes, it's going to

516
00:33:04,059 --> 00:33:06,284
be just like after a bar

