00:35:34,312 --> 00:35:36,112
The buying and selling is evenly matched.

558
00:35:36,412 --> 00:35:38,159
To a lesser extent, the next

559
00:35:38,159 --> 00:35:39,906
bar, you got a positive delta

560
00:35:39,906 --> 00:35:42,819
of 228, which is, you know, kind of a small number.

561
00:35:43,112 --> 00:35:50,712
You know, in the S&Ps, 200 lots, like I said, is one trade, maybe two trades very easily.

562
00:35:50,712 --> 00:35:53,512
You know, that's a market that can trade 200, 300 in a clip.

563
00:35:54,512 --> 00:35:59,712
Then the next bar, you got a delta of negative 18, which again is very small.

564
00:36:00,212 --> 00:36:06,512
You'll see what's happened is you have these three bars with relatively flat delta.

565
00:36:07,212 --> 00:36:08,912
It is positive, 228.

566
00:36:09,512 --> 00:36:15,312
But you net all these together, it's over 17,000, 14,000, 6,000.

567
00:36:15,812 --> 00:36:21,012
You're talking close to 40,000 lots traded in this time period between 9.50.

568
00:36:21,812 --> 00:36:28,212
7 and 10 o'clock and your delta is only 200, it's telling you the market is going sideways.

569
00:36:28,212 --> 00:36:30,712
This is a level where people are happy to transact.

570
00:36:31,112 --> 00:36:32,756
So what you want to do is you

571
00:36:32,756 --> 00:36:34,194
want to watch as the market starts

572
00:36:34,194 --> 00:36:35,221
to move out of this

573
00:36:35,221 --> 00:36:36,248
